<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids down, selling slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids down, selling slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A drop in MGE spring wheat futures sent cash spring wheat bids lower and effectively halted farmer selling, several cash merchants said.</p>
<p>&quot;We bought a fair amount of wheat yesterday but today with the market being down we didn't buy anything,&quot; a Montana dealer said.</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures fell seven cents per bushel and cash bids fell by at least that much in many country locations.</p>
<p>&quot;We got wheat to $4 per bushel to the farmer and that got a lot of wheat moving,&quot; a Minnesota dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;It didn't take much movement to drop (futures prices) back down,&quot; he added.  </p>
